#!/bin/sh
# pipeos-sync-media — push the freshly built pipeos repo onto the boot
# media: verified, atomic, self-reverting. The ONLY sanctioned repo->media
# path on a live box; ad-hoc cp is how the 2026-08-05 incident happened.
#
# Flow: verify source -> stage complete copy next to the live dir (same
# vfat) -> verify the staged copy -> two-rename swap -> apk update +
# fix --simulate against the swapped repo -> on any failure swap back.

SRC=/work/repos/pipeOS/out/repo/pipeos/x86_64
DST=/media/usb/apks/pipeos
VERIFY=/work/repos/pipeOS/scripts/verify-repo.sh

die() { echo "pipeos-sync-media: $*" >&2; exit 1; }

[ -f "$SRC/APKINDEX.tar.gz" ] || die "no built repo at $SRC — run make apks"
[ -x "$VERIFY" ] || die "missing $VERIFY"

"$VERIFY" "$SRC" || die "source repo failed verification; not touching media"

# one media mutator at a time (shared with pipeos-save/rollback)
exec 9> /run/pipeos-save.lock
_i=0
until flock -n 9; do
    _i=$((_i+1)); [ "$_i" -ge 60 ] && die "save lock busy for 60s"; sleep 1
done

mount -o remount,rw /media/usb || die "cannot remount media rw"
finish() { sync; mount -o remount,ro /media/usb 2>/dev/null; }

rm -rf "$DST.new" "$DST.old"
mkdir -p "$DST.new/x86_64" || { finish; die "cannot stage on media"; }
if ! cp "$SRC"/*.apk "$SRC/APKINDEX.tar.gz" "$DST.new/x86_64/"; then
    rm -rf "$DST.new"; finish; die "copy to media failed (space?)"
fi
# initramfs discovers repos by this marker on any boot device
touch "$DST.new/.boot_repository"
sync
"$VERIFY" "$DST.new/x86_64" || { rm -rf "$DST.new"; finish; die "staged copy failed verification"; }

mv "$DST" "$DST.old" && mv "$DST.new" "$DST"
sync

apk update >/dev/null 2>&1
if apk fix --simulate >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    rm -rf "$DST.old"
    finish
    echo "media pipeos repo synced and verified."
    echo "next: pipeos verify && pipeos save"
else
    mv "$DST" "$DST.failed" && mv "$DST.old" "$DST"
    sync
    rm -rf "$DST.failed"
    apk update >/dev/null 2>&1
    finish
    die "world stopped resolving against the new repo — swapped back"
fi
